  "resolves": "e3bed6e6 / ws-20261115.json audit_followups: ordinary command/port/node-allocation pressure does not exhaust the existing embedded xrtNetPost lifecycle channel. No replacement scheduler, retry timer, worker thread or shared runtime is required for this condition.",
  "implementation_facts": [
    "xrtNetEnginePost allocates an ordinary command node and uses the bounded Commands MPSC queue. xrtNetPost embeds its node in caller-owned storage and uses __xrtNetEnginePostInternal, independent of that capacity and allocator.",
    "For valid distinct nodes on a running/unsealed Worker, public command saturation and ordinary post allocation OOM are not xrtNetPost admission failures. Invalid/misused/already-pending nodes and stopped/sealed Workers remain errors. RPC private Posted+Gate and actual post references preserve the required ownership.",
    "Pending clears before the callback begins; false is not a physical callback join. Existing Core callback-repost regression and new callback observations verify this."
  ],
  "verification": "Per host:9 focused WS/WSS modular/single/full-product-selection resource programs,4 select/native-backend public/production-TU saturation programs,1 existing Core embedded-post/repost lifecycle regression. Windows14; WSL15 adds targeted TSan. WSL functional/extra/Core runs use ASan+UBSan+leak halt. Force Windows select/IOCP and WSL select/epoll. No timing release or native72h acceptance.",
  "scope": [
    "Host CommandCapacity2, PortPostLimit1 and NodeCacheBytes0. Verify actual third ordinary post rejection (AGAIN), second port post rejection (AGAIN), ordinary post allocation rejection under budget1 (MEMORY), embedded admission with zero requested heap and exact one queued credit.",
    "Both WS/WSS constructors have full ordinary queues at attach. First calls, Close, original zero deadlines, queued cancellation and notifications progress automatically; typed futures complete before any physical Peer Poll/Wait cleanup nudges. Exact echoed content and exact admitted callback counts survive host joins.",
    "Production-TU probe intercepts only the real xrtNetPost boundary of an incoming-only peer: fill actual queues and invoke real embedded admission under budget1; no mocked success/failure. Exact one inbound execution/reply, zero peer post failures and no replay.",
    "Constructor/encoding/native IO/jobs retain their allocation contracts: budget1 covers embedded admission, not whole constructors or process-wide OOM. Keep the host Engine running through retirement; this stage does not promise operation after host shutdown."
  ],
